+QCY EXECUTABLE PROFILE 1 — implemented contract, not a claim of a general-purpose language
+
+program := metadata{3} Ω ⟦ declaration (',' declaration)* ⟧ '{' statement+ '}' EOF
+metadata := (§λ | §ω | §κ) '(' quoted-nonempty-string ')'
+Each metadata tag occurs exactly once. Canonical layer is checked; strings are data.
+declaration := identifier ':' ℝ '[' positive-integer [',' positive-integer] ']'
+statement := identifier ← expression | ⊢ expression '==' expression
+expression := additive expression with left association, multiplicative expressions,
+              parentheses, finite decimal/scientific literals, flat vector literals,
+              initialized symbol references, unary '-', φ₊(x), φτ(x), φσ(x), ∑(x)
+Multiplicative operators: '*', '/', '⋅' (matrix contraction), '⊗' (Kronecker).
+Additive operators: '+', '-', '⊕'. Multiplicative operators bind more tightly.
+Flat literal assignment to a declared matrix uses row-major order; shape is explicit.
+One assignment per declared name. Reassignment, undeclared output and implicit inputs
+are errors. Every declaration must be initialized. An alias is not an independent input.
+Only a directly assigned literal creates an independently updateable replay input.
+For a negative scalar replay input, initialize it as a one-element literal, e.g. [-1].
+Every program requires an executable equality assertion. Equality uses finite fp64
+numeric equality (signed zero compares equal); cache reuse instead requires equal bits.
+Assertions check concrete runs, not universal propositions or ground-state certificates.
+
+Finite float64 only; ranks 1 and 2; scalar shape [1]. Elementwise scalar broadcasting
+is supported; no other implicit broadcasting, shape clipping or symbolic dimensions.
+No fast-math, no reassociation, no FMA contraction. A nonfinite intermediate or division
+by zero is a runtime error. Only same-op/same-ordered-operands expression reuse is allowed.
+Strict fp64 arithmetic is not exact real arithmetic, algebraic 0-ULP certification or a
+universal guarantee across different compilers, architectures or libm implementations.
+
+UTF-8 is validated, including overlong sequences, surrogates and maximum code point.
+Bidi controls and selected invisible characters are rejected. Names compare by bytes;
+Unicode NFC normalization and universal homoglyph detection are NOT implemented.
+Comments begin with # or // outside strings. Metadata strings cannot contain escapes
+or control characters. Statements may span lines; all tokens must be consumed.
+
+Budgets: source 1 MiB, 400 physical lines; expression nesting 64; 256 declarations;
+4096 IR nodes; tensor 2^20 elements; numeric payload 8 MiB with 64 MiB reservation
+for current values, saved transaction and rollback staging. This is not an RSS limit:
+allocator, compiler, JIT, strings and container overhead are additional.
+A contraction has at most 100 million scalar multiply/add iterations.
+Replay accepts at most 10,000 events in a bounded source file. Only the last committed
+transaction is retained for undo. Failed events restore values and retain prior undo.
+No heuristic arithmetic reordering occurs in incremental propagation. Nodes are visited
+in topological order; propagation stops when the exact cached output bits are unchanged.
+
+Backends: run = typed-IR interpreter; compile-native = C++23 straight-line IR lowering;
+jit = actual compiler invocation, dynamic loading, execution, unloading and temp cleanup.
+JIT compilation is synchronous and is not OSR, a speculative optimizer, or a sandbox.
+Compilation latency is part of JIT end-to-end cost. Native outputs retain assertions.
+verify/enforce typecheck only, and explicitly report that assertions were not executed.
+verify-all is a small executable smoke check, not a scientific release certificate.
+
+Not admitted: complex/quantum values, general control flow/functions, symbolic dimensions,
+implicit agent actions, unbound quantum operators, general reverse-mode differentiation,
+distributed transport, unbounded streams, arbitrary external effects or hardware claims.
+These are rejected or reported unavailable; they are not replaced with demonstration values.
+The legacy scientific/ERA implementations remain preserved separately as research source.
