@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Release acceptance scope: qcy-executable-1
+
+The release builder copies every active source file into a private staging directory,
+verifies SHA-256 against the pre-copy source manifest, removes source write permission,
+builds from those copies, executes independent-answer/backend/negative/transaction checks,
+runs deterministic runtime invariants with ASan+UBSan, and verifies the source hashes again.
+Only then is a stripped, locally ad-hoc-signed binary published under a content/toolchain
+hash. The entrypoint link is replaced atomically. Native/JIT headers are resolved from
+the actual frozen binary location, not from the mutable live checkout.
+
+The signature is local binary integrity, NOT a third-party certification, scientific
+breakthrough certification, patent opinion or proof of general language completeness.
+The copied runtime sources are immutable by convention and file permissions; the owner
+can still alter permissions. Check source.manifest and binary.manifest to detect changes.
+Toolchain and OS are recorded, not bundled. This is a frozen-source build, not a claim of
+bit-reproducible cross-platform builds or a fully hermetic SDK/container.
+
+Unsupported historical .qcy programs fail under the new profile rather than returning
+fabricated traces. Old experiments are retained as historical source and are not linked
+into this release. Their historical report numbers are not release evidence.
+General quantum/compiler/graphics/agent/distributed capabilities require real bindings,
+separate contracts, independent validation and compatibility work before they can graduate.
